It seems you are just trying to figure out which is right position and
which is right note.  Once you get a pattern which gives you a response,
try permuting the notes you played.  Eventually you will get the equivalent
of all white pegs (correct notes in incorrect positions).  Whichever is
more prevalent, the clicks or the gears, should be the white peg.

I've never gotten this far, nor read a spoiler on it, but I might stab
at it this way for first assumptions:  if you get something absolutely
right, something clicks.  If it's close, you're only grinding a few
gears.  The idea above should give you a better conclusion.

